  "@type": "DefinedTerm",
  "alternateName": "Demographic characteristics of a healthy population not affected adversely by anthropogenic pressures",
  "description": "The population demographic characteristics (e.g. body size or age class structure,\nsex ratio, fecundity, and survival rates) of\nthe species are indicative of a healthy population which is not adversely affected\ndue to anthropogenic pressures.\nMember States shall establish threshold\nvalues for specified characteristics of each\nspecies through regional or subregional\ncooperation, taking account of adverse effects on their health derived from D8C2,\nD8C4 and other relevant pressures.",
  "disambiguatingDescription": "This term was created by MBO WP1 task 1.3 with external domain experts during the MARCO-BOLO Project to express that this object is of relevance to the named criterion of the MFSD",
